   "text": "The wall coat hook is built and passes all six plan checks. It is a 30 by 80 by 5 mm back plate with two countersunk M4 holes, and a 16 mm round arm that tapers to 8 mm at the tip and curves up at the end. Nothing is sliced or sent to the printer yet.\n\nThe overall reach is 60 mm to the outer edge of the tip. Sizes I guessed, which you can confirm or change:\n- **Countersink:** 8.5 mm head at 90 degrees, on the arm side so the screw heads sit flush at the front. The 4.5 mm hole is the M4 normal clearance from the Albany County Fasteners chart.\n- **Hole spacing:** 50 mm center to center, 15 mm from the top and bottom edges.\n- **Bend:** 15 mm radius, so the tip rises 15 mm above the arm root.\n\nTell me if the screw is not an M4 flat head, or if you want a different bend radius or hole spacing, and I'll change it. When you want it printed, I can slice it on your P1S with PLA."
